items.prompt:
Take $L = (e^{xy} - 1)^2$ at $x = 0.5$ and $y = 0.8$, with one box per operation: a product, an exponential, a sum with the constant $-1$, and a square. Work it by hand and give:
- (a) every forward value;
- (b) every local derivative at those values;
- (c) every gradient from $L$ back to $x$ and $y$, one box per line;
- (d) a nudge check of $\partial L/\partial x$: move $x$ by 0.01, recompute $L$, and compare.

Optional, one more point: say why the nudge and the gradient differ slightly.
